{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And clay:</b> Some say it is from נגששה כעורים (groping like the blind). Others said it is a species of creature. The nearer [meaning] is that it is a kind of dust, as in מישני אדמת עפר יקיצו (they will awaken from the dust of the earth)." "<b>רגע:</b> R. Moses said: split open, and like it על רגעי ארץ רגע אחד ממנו, and its meaning is a portion. He said that וימאס is from נמס, and the alef is in place of the samekh, like the alef in זאו נהרים. What is correct in my eyes: that רגע is from רוגע הים (the sea's roaring), and וימאס is according to its [usual] meaning, because it changed."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:04.414951003Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}